==Russian==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ru|пздц||texting or internet slang}}
* {{alt|ru|3.14здец||texting or internet slang}}

===Etymology===
{{af|ru|пизда́|-ец}}, attested since ca. 1973<!--https://books.google.com/books?id=6UkeAQAAMAAJ&q=%D0%BF%D0%B8%D0%B7%D0%B4%D0%B5%D1%86-->. Compare {{cog|uk|пизде́ць}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ru-IPA|пизде́ц}}
** {{audio|ru|Ru-пиздец.ogg}}
* {{IPA|ru|[pʲizʲˈdʲet͡s]|a=Southern Russia}}
* {{IPA|ru|[pʲizʲˈd͡zʲet͡s]|a=Belarus}} (''phonetic respelling'': пиздзе́ц)
* {{IPA|ru|[pʲizʲˈdʲɛt͡s]|a=Ukraine}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun+|b|пизде́ц|adj=пиздецо́вый|expr=пиздо́с}} {{tlb|ru|vulgar}}

# extreme amount of something: [[fuckload]], [[shitload]], [[fuckton]], [[shitton]]
#: {{uxi|ru|1 000 000 — [[этот|э́то]] '''пизде́ц''' [[ско́лько]] [[деньги|де́нег]]!|One million is a '''shitload''' of money!}}
# {{lb|ru|sometimes|humorous}} [[clusterfuck]], [[shitshow]] {{gloss|[[extremely]] [[undesirable]] situation}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-table|b|пизде́ц}}

===Predicative===
{{head|ru|predicative|head=пизде́ц}}

# {{lb|ru|vulgar}} [[death]], [[curtains]]; [[screwed]], [[fucked]]
#: {{uxi|ru|ему́ '''пизде́ц'''!|he is fucked!}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ru|ппц}}
* {{l|ru|коне́ц}} {{qualifier|neutral}}
* {{l|ru|кранты́}}, {{l|ru|хана́}}, {{l|ru|каю́к}}, {{l|ru|кирды́к}}, {{l|ru|кры́шка}}, {{l|ru|капу́т}} {{qualifier|colloquial}}

; Euphemisms
*corruptions: {{l|ru|пипе́ц}}, {{l|ru|писе́ц}}, {{l|ru|песе́ц}}, {{l|ru|абза́ц}}
*various descriptions of 'песец': {{m|ru||маленький пушной зверек|little fur animal}}, {{m|ru||маленький северный лис|little polar fox}}, etc.
*portmanteaus: {{l|ru|кранде́ц}}, {{l|ru|кабзде́ц}}, {{l|ru|трынде́ц}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ru|по́лный пизде́ц}}
* {{l|ru|пиздецо́ма}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|kk|пиздес|bor=1}}, {{l|kk|пездес}}

===Interjection===
{{head|ru|interjection|head=пизде́ц}}

# {{lb|ru|vulgar}} [[fucking hell]]!, [[holy shit]]!, [[what the fuck]]!

====Usage notes====
{{m|ru|ппц}}, pronounced as {{m|ru|пипе́ц}}, is understood among people familiar with phones and PCs.

